  speakerName: RONNIE
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'When meeting someone new, one of the first things you may want to
    know is their name.


    In Ilokano, ''ania ti nagan mo?'' means ''what is your
    name?''


    You can use this phrase when introducing yourself to someone or
    asking for their name.


    Listen carefully: ania ti nagan mo?


    Now, try
    saying ''ania ti nagan mo?'' yourself.'
